    "execution": {"startingPosition": "Log one dumbbell's weight, not the pair total. Stand tall with one matching dumbbell beside each thigh and room to travel forward.", "movement": "Step forward with one leg, lower under control into a split stance, then drive through the lead foot and carry the trail leg directly into the next forward step.", "endpoint": "Finish each repetition as the opposite foot lands ahead to begin the next lunge; do not stop in a feet-together stance.", "returnPhase": "Continue forward by alternating lead legs for the prescribed repetitions.", "controlledJoints": "Keep the dumbbells still, wrists neutral, trunk braced, and each lead knee tracking over the foot.", "supportAndPosture": "Use no hand support and do not push the dumbbells with body swing.", "disqualifyingCompensations": ["Returning to feet-together standing after every step turns the task into step-and-return lunges.", "Repeating one lead leg leaves the alternating walking fixture.", "Jumping between stances turns the exercise into a jumping lunge."], "sideOrDirection": "Alternate lead legs continuously while traveling forward; count each completed step as one repetition."}
